# Build parallelism

When building the game with `make` (or any Make-based build in this repo), always pass **`-j$(nproc)`** so the build uses all available CPU cores.

- **Do**: `make -j$(nproc)` or `make -j$(nproc) debug`, etc.
- **Do not**: use a fixed job count like `-j4`; that underutilizes multi-core machines.

This applies to the main Crawl build from `crawl-ref/source/` and to any recursive or contrib builds that use make.
